Sections "COLLECTION" contain missmatched items: {'COLLECTION_SUMMARY': ["Subjects were recruited from the CLIMB study at the Brigham and Women's Hospital (BWH) MS Center. All protocols were approved by the BWH Institutional Review Board (IRB Protocol #2017P001169) and informed consent was obtained from every study subject. Inclusion criteria: a diagnosis of MS according to the latest McDonald criteria, with primary and secondary progressive MS grouped together. Exclusion criteria: current pregnancy, gastrointestinal surgical history, gastrointestinal disease, or antibiotic use within 3 months prior to sampling. Healthy control samples were obtained from healthy subjects in the PhenoGenetic Project; collection and processing procedures for these samples were identical to those for MS participants. Progression independent of relapse activity (PIRA) was not quantified in these subjects. Dietary information was not collected at the time of sampling. Sample collection: paired serum and stool samples from a given subject were collected within +/- 45 days of each other. Serum samples were frozen and stored at -80 C from the time of collection until shipment. Cognitive and quality-of-life testing (SDMT, CVLT-II, Neuro-QoL), where performed, was carried out within 6 months of stool and blood donation. Samples were shipped on dry ice to Metabolon Inc. (Morrisville, NC, USA), which received 88 serum samples on May 25, 2023; on receipt, samples were inventoried, accessioned into the Metabolon LIMS, and maintained at -80 C until extraction. The paired fecal samples from this cohort are deposited separately (DATATRACK ID 4916). Explanation of the codes used in the GROUP column of the study design table: HC = Healthy Control (PhenoGenetic Project). StRRMS = Stable relapsing-remitting MS; RRMS at baseline that remained relapsing-remitting at 2-year follow-up. TRRMS = Transitioned relapsing-remitting MS; RRMS at baseline that transitioned to secondary progressive MS by 2-year follow-up. Transition was classified by the treating clinician's diagnosis, based on continued worsening of the standard neurological exam and increasing EDSS. ProgMS = Progressive MS at baseline (primary and secondary progressive MS grouped together), matched to the other groups on age, sex, race/ethnicity, and disease-modifying therapy (DMT) use.", "Subjects were recruited from the CLIMB study at the Brigham and Women''s Hospital (BWH) MS Center. All protocols were approved by the BWH Institutional Review Board (IRB Protocol #2017P001169) and informed consent was obtained from every study subject. Inclusion criteria: a diagnosis of MS according to the latest McDonald criteria, with primary and secondary progressive MS grouped together. Exclusion criteria: current pregnancy, gastrointestinal surgical history, gastrointestinal disease, or antibiotic use within 3 months prior to sampling. Healthy control samples were obtained from healthy subjects in the PhenoGenetic Project; collection and processing procedures for these samples were identical to those for MS participants. Progression independent of relapse activity (PIRA) was not quantified in these subjects. Dietary information was not collected at the time of sampling. Sample collection: paired serum and stool samples from a given subject were collected within +/- 45 days of each other. Serum samples were frozen and stored at -80 C from the time of collection until shipment. Cognitive and quality-of-life testing (SDMT, CVLT-II, Neuro-QoL), where performed, was carried out within 6 months of stool and blood donation. Samples were shipped on dry ice to Metabolon Inc. (Morrisville, NC, USA), which received 88 serum samples on May 25, 2023; on receipt, samples were inventoried, accessioned into the Metabolon LIMS, and maintained at -80 C until extraction. The paired fecal samples from this cohort are deposited separately (DATATRACK ID 4916). Explanation of the codes used in the GROUP column of the study design table: HC = Healthy Control (PhenoGenetic Project). StRRMS = Stable relapsing-remitting MS; RRMS at baseline that remained relapsing-remitting at 2-year follow-up. TRRMS = Transitioned relapsing-remitting MS; RRMS at baseline that transitioned to secondary progressive MS by 2-year follow-up. Transition was classified by the treating clinician''s diagnosis, based on continued worsening of the standard neurological exam and increasing EDSS. ProgMS = Progressive MS at baseline (primary and secondary progressive MS grouped together), matched to the other groups on age, sex, race/ethnicity, and disease-modifying therapy (DMT) use."]}
